<title>PAKISTAN: Moderate quake jolts southwest Pakistan.</title>
<headline>Moderate quake jolts southwest Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A moderate earthquake rocked southwestern Pakistan on Thursday, but there was no immediate report of damage or casualties, officials said.</p>
<p>A government seismic centre said the quake, which measured 5.5 on the Richter scale, shook the Baluchistan provincial capital of Quetta and nearby areas. A more powerful tremor in the same region on February 28 killed about 50 people.</p>
